Vector Calculus — David Tong (@em-vector-book: 0, is #reference, #part-of @em-sources) { r_2YD2PDK99N62GBWKXXCBY69PP5
David Tong. [Author's full first-year Vector Calculus course](https://davidtong.org/teaching/vector-calculus/).

Read the complete notes and work the examples on curves and surfaces, coordinate systems, gradient/divergence/curl, integral theorems, partial differential equations and tensors. Revisit the exact sections at the field equations; the whole course is an available mathematical foundation rather than an unspoken assumption that a beginner already knows it.

The author offers an approximately 120-page course through the current teaching page. Its identity and contents were checked on 29 October 2026. Author-hosted free access is not a general reuse licence; no commercial-book appendix or course file is copied here. Mathematical proofs should be reconstructed and tested on independently chosen fields.

